  "id": "COMPOUND:17991 - PROTEIN:1478",
  "verbalization": "Cyclohexanol, 2-methylene-5-(1-methylethenyl)-, (1S-cis)- is implicated in the target pathway leading to Sodium channel protein type 11 subunit alpha through multiple indirect routes. The evidence suggests that this compound acts as a target for several kinase inhibitors, including Amidepsine D and 1,3-Diphenylpropan-1-One, which are themselves targets of other compounds. These inhibitors are known to modulate sodium channel activity, which is a key mechanism in the regulation of neuronal excitability. The presence of multiple pathways converging on the sodium channel protein type 11 subunit alpha indicates a potential role for Cyclohexanol in influencing sodium channel function, possibly through the inhibition of kinases that regulate these channels. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Cyclohexanol may exert its effects on sodium channels, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
